# Client app repo hygiene (all factory projects)

Applies to **every** product repo delivered via this engine / sibling agents.

## Ownership

| Asset | Where it lives | In customer git? |
|-------|----------------|------------------|
| Factory skills (`dev-*`, BA/UX/QA kicks) | Engine (`.cursor/skills/`) | **Never** |
| Stack marketplace packs | Engine `.agents/skills` via `sync_stack_skills.sh` + `verify_stack_skills.sh` | **Never** |
| Project-only / conflicting **skills** | `projects/<slug>/.cursor/skills/` (gitignored) | **Never** |
| Skill install / verify scripts | Engine `scripts/` only | **Never** in app |
| Links to skills.sh / skill GitHub packs / engine skill paths | Engine docs only | **Never** in app |
| **Product process rules** (labels, BA/UX sentinels, Themis, CR) | App `.cursor/rules/` (e.g. `factory-*.mdc`, `code-review.mdc`) | **Yes — required for enforcement in the app workspace** |
| Product code, OpenSpec product specs, CI, deploy | App repo | Yes |
| OpenSpec workflow skills (`openspec-*`) | App `.cursor/skills/openspec-*` or host | Yes (product tooling) |
| Product engineering standards | `docs/CODE_STANDARDS.md` (+ `code-review.mdc`) | Yes |

## Why product rules stay in the app

Agents often open the **app** as the Cursor workspace. Rules only under
`projects/<slug>/` in the engine are **not** auto-loaded there. Label gates
(`ba-spec-first`, `ux-charter-first`, `BA_SPEC_READY`, …) must live in the app
so they are visible and enforceable. Skills still attach from the engine via
manifest + Read.

## Absolute forbidden in app repos (tracked files)

- `.cursor/skills/*` **except** `openspec-*`; any `.agents/skills/`
- `docs/SKILLS*.md`, skill install runbooks, `scripts/sync_*skills*`
- Rules that wire stack-skill install (`*skill*.mdc`) or link marketplace skill URLs
- Seat playbooks / AGENT-PREP that expose internal engine skill maps (keep under `projects/<slug>/docs` if needed)

## Allowed in app `.cursor/rules/`

- `code-review.mdc` — product engineering constraints
- `factory-*.mdc` — **this product’s** delivery gates (labels, sentinels, review)
- Other product-local process rules that do **not** reference skill packs / engine skill paths

## How agents attach stack skills

1. Read `projects/<slug>/project.yaml` → `stack.*`
2. Engine: `bash scripts/verify_stack_skills.sh <slug> [--install]`
3. **Read** every path in `projects/<slug>/factory/stack-skills.manifest`
4. Implement in the **app** working tree — never copy packs into the app
5. Obey app `.cursor/rules/factory-*.mdc` + `code-review.mdc` while implementing

## What the client may receive

- Source, tests, OpenSpec **product** specs, CI/deploy
- Product process rules + CODE_STANDARDS (how *this* product is built)
- **Not** our skill catalog, install scripts, or marketplace skill URLs

If unsure about a **skill** file: keep it in the engine.  
If unsure about a **process gate** for this product: prefer the **app** `.cursor/rules/`.
